The code compiles cleanly.

**Analysis:**
- **Module A:** `z = (x ^ y) & x`
- **Module B:** From the waveform, `z = 1` only when `x == y` → `z = ~(x ^ y)` (XNOR)
- **Top:** `or_out = A1 | B1`, `and_out = A2 & B2`, `z = or_out ^ and_out` (which reduces to `x | ~y`)

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  wire x,
    input  wire y,
    output wire z
);

    // Module A instances: z = (x ^ y) & x
    wire a1 = (x ^ y) & x;
    wire a2 = (x ^ y) & x;

    // Module B instances (derived from waveform): z = ~(x ^ y)  (XNOR)
    wire b1 = ~(x ^ y);
    wire b2 = ~(x ^ y);

    // First pair -> OR gate
    wire or_out  = a1 | b1;

    // Second pair -> AND gate
    wire and_out = a2 & b2;

    // OR and AND outputs -> XOR gate -> z
    assign z = or_out ^ and_out;

endmodule
```
